- Test: `03-ai-rag-engine/tests/test_vector_store.py`

**Interfaces:**
- Produces: batch `Embedder` protocol, one benchmark-selected production provider, persistent Qdrant index adapter, and index-build measurements.
- Guarantees: metadata preservation, idempotent upserts, configurable model, precomputed corpus embeddings.

- [ ] Benchmark genuinely multilingual candidates in the shared cross-lingual space before selecting one.
- [x] Implement the provider/store boundary, deterministic fixture baseline, and optional injected Qdrant adapter without selecting a production winner.
- [x] Verify local point count, metadata, resume/reconciliation behavior, and fixture index-build measurements.

**Verified 2026-08-22:** 19 focused embedding/index tests and the full 68-test engine suite pass; `compileall`, index CLI help, and scoped `git diff --check` succeed. Local snapshots are versioned and atomic, resume fails closed on provider/config changes, stale chunks are reconciled, and the optional Qdrant adapter uses deterministic UUID point IDs. The real multilingual provider benchmark, production winner, live Qdrant validation, ADR 0002, and ADR 0005 remain open external gates.

### Task 4: Top-K Retrieval and Reranking

**Files:**
- Modify: `03-ai-rag-engine/retrieval/retriever.py`
- Modify: `03-ai-rag-engine/retrieval/reranker.py`
- Modify: `06-evaluation/metrics/retrieval.py`
- Modify: `06-evaluation/benchmarks/retrieval.py`
- Test: `03-ai-rag-engine/tests/test_retrieval.py`

**Interfaces:**
- Produces: `retrieve(query, top_k)` returning chunk ID, text, score, metadata, and latency; optional reranking from broad candidates to final evidence.
- Guarantees: retrieval quality is measured before generation is connected.

- [x] Add Recall@k, MRR@k, and graded nDCG@k fixtures with monolingual/cross-lingual and per-query-locale breakdowns.
- [x] Measure local fixture reranking gain against its latency cost without selecting a winner.
- [ ] Freeze retrieval and reranker decisions in ADRs before moving on.

**Verified 2026-08-22:** 13 focused retrieval tests and the full 68-test engine suite pass; compilation, benchmark smoke, and scoped diff checks succeed. Retrieval enforces `top_k` 1..20, hard-bounds reranking candidates by `fetch_k`, validates payload/reranker identity, and reports embedding/search/reranking/total latency. The fixture benchmark reports quality and latency deltas only; the real multilingual retrieval/reranker benchmark and ADR 0004 remain open.

